      <article class="prose">
        <p>Hersham railway station serves Hersham, Walton Park and the Field Common area of Surrey. It sits on the South West Main Line, roughly 15 miles 73 chains from London Waterloo, which is a little under 16 miles. South Western Railway manages the station and runs its trains, and the station code is <strong>HER</strong>.</p>

        <p>It is a small, plain station, and the single most important thing to know about it is that you cannot reach either platform without using stairs.</p>

        <blockquote class="alert">
          <p><strong>There is no step-free access at Hersham.</strong> National Rail and South Western Railway both classify it as a <strong>step-free category C</strong> station, meaning no step-free access to any part of it. Both platforms are above street level and reached by stairs, and there are no lifts. If you cannot use stairs, see <a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a> below before you travel.</p>
        </blockquote>

        <p><a href="https://www.nationalrail.co.uk/live-trains/departures/hersham/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check live departures from Hersham ↗</a></p>

        <blockquote>
          <p><strong>Checked against National Rail, South Western Railway, Elmbridge Borough Council and ORR:</strong> August 2026. Ticket office hours, bus times and car park charges all change; each section links the official source so you can confirm before you travel.</p>
        </blockquote>

